        {
          "id": 825521907,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Your contributions are welcome, thank you. It's impossible to know everything beforehand, that is why we have reviews. It's an interactive process, which should result in quality contributions.\nAs for the size of contributions, that is hard to tell. To help the review, make them as small as possible, preferably on a single topic, while still being complete within itself. E.g., for a protocol with lots of PDU's, start off the basic structure of the dissector and add dissection of the PDU's details in later merge requests.",
